(e) Workflow
    1. Loaded capital.csv (decimal=","), time_series_data.csv, and pollen_openness_*.csv (also German decimal).
    2. Built SC3 = Z(CuAu) + Z(Amber) + Z(MonumentCount) for every 100y CE bin from capital.csv raw Z.
    3. Cross-checked by aggregating time_series_data.*_inter bin-means to identical 100y CE bins.
    4. Computed sensitivity variants SC_mean_3, SC_4 (+MonumentSize), SC_3_dt (within-phase detrended).
    5. Identified two adjacent OBA bins tied at SC3 = +4.24σ (BCE 1400 and BCE 1300); reported as contiguous plateau window 1500–1300 BCE.
    6. Computed prior trough on active (non-prefilled) data → LN phase (BCE 2000/1900, SC3 ≈ −1.86σ).
    7. Computed per-component ΔZ over the 2-bin lead window (BCE 1600 and 1500) vs peak plateau.
    8. Sampled pollen-based openness (Belau_PC1_inter, MEAN) at the peak vs prior century for cross-check.

